Check out http://spanish-nethack.sourceforge.net/ .  But don't take the
translations as gospel, at least in the main code.

Some of the technical issues, in particular character set support, would work
well enough for a French NetHack.  Others would of course have to be reworked. 
Some of the grammatical bits could be brought over with a little work. 
Different pluralization rules, gender, mandatory contractions (by which I mean
de le -> du, de les -> des, le and la losing their vowels before another vowel),
and having to pluralize the adjectives would all have to be dealt with.  Your
final code might look more like the Spanish code than the English, but will
likely be different from both.

Expect to be done with the main code in several months if you keep at it.

Roguelikes are difficult to internationalize the right way, with separately
distributed locale data and a message catalogue for the translation, because
they assemble bits and pieces of text into complete sentences in a variety of
ways.  I know of no roguelike that is properly internationalized.

